# A1/A1.1/A1_01_greetings.letz
# Source: Quizlet "A1 Basics Beginner Luxembourgish Lesson 1"
#   https://quizlet.com/_h2t0v7
# All @word and @sentence content is taken from the Quizlet flashcards.
# Slash variants and bracket alternatives are split into atomic pairs;
# (formal)/(informal) qualifiers are stripped (LU form already encodes formality).
# Distractor tokens are sourced from other entries within this same Quizlet set.
# @fill added: time-of-day greetings/farewells, dative pronoun frames (ginn + dir/Iech/eis/hinnen),
# hunn vs sinn copula, prepositions (zu/beim/an), and emotion adjectives.

@lesson A1.01 "Greetings"

# --- Greetings (Quizlet cards 1-6, 67) ---
@word Gudde Moien = Good morning
@word Gudde Mëtteg = Good afternoon
@word Gudde Mëtten = Good afternoon
@word Gudden Owend = Good evening
@word Moien = Hi
@word Bonjour = Hello
@word Salut = Hi
@word Wëllkomm = Welcome

# --- Farewells (Quizlet cards 13-22, 38) ---
@word Äddi = Bye
@word Bis geschwënn = See you soon
@word Bis herno = See you later
@word Bis muer = See you tomorrow
@word Bis dann = See you later
@word Bis muer de Moien = See you tomorrow morning
@word Bis de Mëtteg = See you at noon
@word Bis de Mëtteg = See you in the afternoon
@word Bis de Mëtten = See you at noon
@word Bis de Mëtten = See you in the afternoon
@word Bis den Owend = See you in the evening
@word Gutt Nuecht = Good night

# --- Politeness (Quizlet cards 34-37, 55-57) ---
@word Merci = Thank you
@word Ganz gutt = Very good
@word Entschëllegt = Excuse me
@word Pardon = Sorry
@word Wannechgelift = Please
@word Jo = Yes
@word Nee = No

# --- Vocabulary from sentences (coverage backfill) ---
@word d'Zäit = time
@word d'Glas = glass
@word d'Waasser = water
@word de Kaffi = coffee
@word den Zocker = sugar
@word d'Stéck = piece
@word d'Zitroun = lemon
@word kleng = small
@word traureg = sad
@word frou = happy
@word hongereg = hungry
@word sauer = sour
@word alles = everything
@word eppes = something
@word vill = a lot
@word gär = gladly
@word drénken = to drink
@word hëllefen = to help
@word kréien = to get
@word soen = to say

# --- Sentences (Quizlet cards 7-12, 23-33, 39-54, 58-66, 68) ---

@sentence
@lu Moien, wéi geet et?
@en Hi, how are you?
@distractor-en evening
@distractor-en morning
@distractor-en where
@distractor-lu Äddi
@distractor-lu Owend
@distractor-lu Wou

