# --- @fill: time-of-day greetings -----------------------------------------------
# Distractors are sibling time-of-day greetings the learner already knows,
# forcing discrimination between morning/afternoon/evening.

@fill
@lu [Gudde Moien], wëllt Dir e Kaffi drénken? Bis den Owend!
@en [Good morning], would you like to drink a coffee? See you in the evening!
@distractor-lu Gudde Mëtteg
@distractor-lu Gudden Owend
@distractor-lu Salut
@distractor-en Good afternoon
@distractor-en Good evening
@distractor-en Hi

@fill
@lu [Gudde Mëtteg], ech sinn de Tom aus Lëtzebuerg.
@en [Good afternoon], I'm Tom from Luxembourg.
@distractor-lu Gudde Moien
@distractor-lu Gudden Owend
@distractor-lu Moien
@distractor-en Good morning
@distractor-en Good evening
@distractor-en Hi

@fill
@lu [Gudden Owend], wëllt Dir e Kaffi? Gutt Nuecht!
@en [Good evening], do you want a coffee? Good night!
@distractor-lu Gudde Moien
@distractor-lu Gudde Mëtteg
@distractor-lu Bonjour
@distractor-en Good morning
@distractor-en Good afternoon
@distractor-en Hello

# --- @fill: farewells -----------------------------------------------------------
# Bis + time-word confusion is a genuine A1 pain point. Distractors are
# other farewell time words from this lesson.

@fill
@lu [Bis muer], ech ginn heem. Gutt Nuecht!
@en [See you tomorrow], I'm going home. Good night!
@distractor-lu Bis geschwënn
@distractor-lu Bis den Owend
@distractor-lu Bis herno
@distractor-en See you soon
@distractor-en See you in the evening
@distractor-en See you later

@fill
@lu [Bis geschwënn], ech kommen erëm haut nach.
@en [See you soon], I'm coming back again today.
@distractor-lu Bis muer
@distractor-lu Bis den Owend
@distractor-lu Bis dann
@distractor-en See you tomorrow
@distractor-en See you in the evening
@distractor-en See you later

@fill
@lu [Bis den Owend], mir ginn zesummen iessen.
@en [See you in the evening], we're eating together.
@distractor-lu Bis de Mëtteg
@distractor-lu Bis muer
@distractor-lu Bis geschwënn
@distractor-en See you at noon
@distractor-en See you tomorrow
@distractor-en See you soon

# --- @fill: dative pronoun frames (ginn + indirect object) ----------------------
# The learner picks the correct indirect-object pronoun. Distractors are
# other dative pronouns from the same "Ech ginn X e Bic" paradigm.

@fill
@lu Ech ginn haut [Iech] e Glas Waasser.
@en Today I give [you] a glass of water.
@distractor-lu dir
@distractor-lu eis
@distractor-lu hinnen
@distractor-en us
@distractor-en them
@distractor-en me

@fill
@lu Mir ginn haut [eis] e Kaffi.
@en Today we give [ourselves] a coffee.
@distractor-lu dir
@distractor-lu Iech
@distractor-lu hinnen
@distractor-en you
@distractor-en them
@distractor-en him

@fill
@lu Du gëss [hinnen] e Stéck Schockela.
@en You give [them] a piece of chocolate.
@distractor-lu dir
@distractor-lu eis
@distractor-lu Iech
@distractor-en us
@distractor-en me
@distractor-en you

# --- @fill: hunn vs sinn (copula / auxiliary) -----------------------------------
# The learner confuses "Ech hunn" and "Ech sinn" — the blank is the verb,
# distractors are the other auxiliary or a wrong conjugation.

@fill
@lu Ech [sinn] traureg a kleng.
@en I [am] sad and small.
@distractor-lu hunn
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu gees
@distractor-en have
@distractor-en give
@distractor-en go

@fill
@lu Ech [hunn] e Kaffi a Zocker.
@en I [have] a coffee and sugar.
@distractor-lu sinn
@distractor-lu ginn
@distractor-lu kréien
@distractor-en am
@distractor-en give
@distractor-en get

# --- @fill: prepositions (zu/beim/an) -------------------------------------------
# Prepositions from the sentences this lesson teaches. Determiners stay
# in the frame so correct text never depends on which tile is placed.

@fill
@lu Ech si [zu] Lëtzebuerg.
@en I am [in] Luxembourg.
@distractor-lu bei
@distractor-lu mat
@distractor-lu aus
@distractor-en at
@distractor-en with
@distractor-en from

@fill
@lu Mir si [beim] Dokter.
@en We are [at the] doctor.
@distractor-lu am
@distractor-lu um
@distractor-lu aus dem
@distractor-en in the
@distractor-en on the
@distractor-en from the

# --- @fill: emotion adjectives --------------------------------------------------
# The blank is the predicate adjective after sinn/ass; distractors are
# other emotion/state adjectives from this lesson.

@fill
@lu Ech si [frou] a mir geet et gutt.
@en I am [happy] and I'm fine.
@distractor-lu traureg
@distractor-lu hongereg
@distractor-lu kleng
@distractor-en sad
@distractor-en hungry
@distractor-en small

@fill
@lu Dat ass [sauer], ech drénke Waasser.
@en That is [sour], I'm drinking water.
@distractor-lu kleng
@distractor-lu frou
@distractor-lu traureg
@distractor-en small
@distractor-en happy
@distractor-en sad
